## 4. Standards axis: zero literal escape sequences

Command, run over every `.oo` source in both layers:

```
grep -rlP '\x1b' --include="*.oo" <repo>       # raw 0x1b byte
grep -rlE '\\x1b|\\u\{1b\}|\\033' --include="*.oo" <repo>   # textual escape
```

Zero matches in all 37 repositories. The theme pages emit ANSI through `chr(27)`, which is a real
export of `std/core/primitives/str.oo`.

## 5. Contention analysis for the two reported failures

The first sweep reported `ootaskmgr` and `ooterm` as failing `make verify` and `make test` with
exit code 2. Both were traced to the environment, not to the source:

1. `make verify` reaches the `check` target at `Makefile:124`, which runs `oodac check` once per
   `.oo` page. Each `oodac check` invocation allocates about 1.1 GB.
2. The sweep ran three repositories in parallel while the host load average was 26 on a 12-core
   machine with 32 GB of RAM, and 32 concurrent `emit-llvm` processes were resident. The
   `emit-llvm` step was killed by the kernel.
3. Running `oodac check` over every `.oo` page of `ootaskmgr` one at a time produced zero failures.
4. `make verify` and `make test` then pass standalone in both repositories:
   `ootaskmgr` verify exit 0 and test exit 0 (`ALL TESTS PASSED`), `ooterm` verify exit 0 and
   test exit 0 (`ALL TESTS PASSED`).
5. A fresh clone of `origin/master` for each of the two repositories passes `make verify` with
   exit code 0, which proves the committed tree is sound independently of the local working copy.
6. The same pattern reproduced with `oomail`: `make build` failed with `emit-llvm failed` at load
   average 26, and the identical command succeeded with exit code 0 once the load fell to 5.8.
7. The final sweep, run with two repositories in flight and a load average between 4 and 8, reports
   `build=0 verify=0 test=0` for `ootaskmgr` and `ooterm` like every other repository, and both
   test binaries report `ALL TESTS PASSED`.

No repair was made to either repository, because there is nothing to repair.

## 6. Spec axis: theme contract

Command per repository:

```
<repo>/bin/<repo> theme --json
<repo>/bin/<repo> theme <name> --tui
```

All 37 repositories: `theme --json` parses as JSON and carries all five required keys (`theme`,
`bg_rgba`, `fg_rgba`, `accent_rgba`, `checksum`). Every frame line of `theme <name> --tui` measures
exactly 60 visible columns after the ANSI sequences are stripped, for all five themes (`ooda-dark`,
`ooda-light`, `1982`, `high-contrast`, `no-color`).

## 7. Spec axis: runtime Rule 1.25

All 37 DE and apps binaries:

| Selector | Exit code |
|---|---|
| `--persona` | 2 |
| `--persona=<name>` | 2 |
| `--list-personas` | 2 |
| `--mode` (bare) | 2 |
| `--mode <unknown>` | 2 |
| unknown flag | 2 |

The only `--persona` literals in the DE layer are inside the `persona_banned_flag` refusal helper
(`core/persona/dispatch.oo`), which is what Rule 1.25 requires. The apps layer has zero such
literals. The `--mode <valid persona>` case is recorded as finding F2.

