Command: `grep -rnE '100\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+|zebes|ringmaster|spotlight' --include="*.oo"`

Zero matches in all 37 repositories.

## 9. Git sync state

After the sweep, all 37 repositories report zero commits ahead of and zero commits behind
`origin/master`, except `openOODA-apps/ooflash`, which is one commit behind
(`8ca0b07 test: extend device-safety negative-trust coverage`). That commit passes `make verify`
from a fresh clone of `origin/master` with exit code 0.

### 9.1 The concurrent `std` to `oostd` rename

At 12:56, during the sweep, a fleet-wide rename from `std` to `oostd` landed in the working trees
of every repository in both layers. The on-disk directory `/Projects/openOODA-core/std` was renamed
to `/Projects/openOODA-core/oostd`, and every `.oo` import in the DE and apps layers was rewritten
from `import "std/..."` to `import "oostd/..."`. The rename is uncommitted in the consumer
repositories and is the work of a concurrent session, not of this review.

The committed state on `origin/master` is unaffected and is the state this review verified. Two
facts make the committed state the correct one to keep:

1. The GitHub repository is still `openOODA-core/std`; there is no `openOODA-core/oostd` repository
   (`gh repo view openOODA-core/oostd` returns "Could not resolve to a Repository"). A consumer
   repository that committed `import "oostd/..."` would break every CI runner, which clones
   `openOODA-core/std.git` into `/Projects/openOODA-core/std`.
2. The compiler's `oostd/` prefix fallback is itself an uncommitted working-tree change in
   `openOODA-core/oodac` (`ast/load_import_parse.oo`, modified but not committed; the committed
   `origin/master` of `oodac` contains no `oostd` reference at all). The local `oodac` binary
   resolves both prefixes, which is why the local tree builds either way.

The committed `origin/master` trees import `std/...`, and they build and verify cleanly against
both the old and the new on-disk layout. Verified after the rename: `oowm` builds with exit code 0
and `make verify` passes with exit code 0 from a fresh clone of `origin/master`.

### 9.2 Upstream movement during the review

The concurrent session pushed four commits to every DE repository while this review was in
progress (`8245c75`, `41c0a19`, `445d1b1`, `b8d6a2a` — the theme wiring and its merges). These
were re-verified after the fact: `oowm` at the new `origin/master` passes `make verify` with exit
code 0, and the Batch 4 theme import fix is still present at `origin/master` (`theme/ootheme.oo`
carries no `std/core/primitives/str.oo` import).

